{"id":"a6c20c97a5eba13a","group":"93","path":"93/93-fact-abelian-boolean.md","title":"Abelian Boolean","display":"Abelian Boolean","type":"fact","metadata":{"type":"fact","book":"Algebraizable Logics","book_abbrev":"93","label":"93-fact-abelian-boolean","aliases":["93-fact-abelian-boolean"],"display":"Abelian Boolean","depends_on":["[[93-df-abelian]]","[[93-df-boolean-algebra]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"fact"},{"key":"book","html":"Algebraizable Logics"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"93"},{"key":"label","html":"93-fact-abelian-boolean"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>93-fact-abelian-boolean</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"Abelian Boolean"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"e2be868cf664b716\" href=\"?note=e2be868cf664b716\" title=\"93-df-abelian\">93-df-abelian</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"7087f500cc845c3b\" href=\"?note=7087f500cc845c3b\" title=\"93-df-boolean-algebra\">93-df-boolean-algebra</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{BooleanAlg}_{93}(\\mathbf A)\">\\(\\mathrm{BooleanAlg}_{93}(\\mathbf A)\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\exists a,b\\in|\\mathbf A|\\;(a\\ne b)\">\\(\\exists a,b\\in|\\mathbf A|\\;(a\\ne b)\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"[-,-]\">\\([-,-]\\)</span> is the commutator on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Con}(\\mathbf A)\">\\(\\mathrm{Con}(\\mathbf A)\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{AbAlg}\">\\(\\mathrm{AbAlg}\\)</span> is the abelian-algebra class of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"e2be868cf664b716\" href=\"?note=e2be868cf664b716\" title=\"93-df-abelian\">93-df-abelian</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{fact\\text{-}abelian\\text{-}boolean}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{BooleanAlg}_{93}(\\mathbf A)\\land\\bigl(\\exists a,b\\in|\\mathbf A|\\;(a\\ne b)\\bigr)\n\\to\\mathbf A\\notin\\mathrm{AbAlg}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{fact\\text{-}abelian\\text{-}boolean}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{BooleanAlg}_{93}(\\mathbf A)\\land\\bigl(\\exists a,b\\in|\\mathbf A|\\;(a\\ne b)\\bigr)\n\\to\\mathbf A\\notin\\mathrm{AbAlg}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>In a Boolean algebra the congruence commutator is meet, hence\n<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"[\\nabla_{\\mathbf A},\\nabla_{\\mathbf A}]_{\\mathbf A}=\\nabla_{\\mathbf A}\">\\([\\nabla_{\\mathbf A},\\nabla_{\\mathbf A}]_{\\mathbf A}=\\nabla_{\\mathbf A}\\)</span>.  For a\nnontrivial algebra this is not <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Delta_{\\mathbf A}\">\\(\\Delta_{\\mathbf A}\\)</span>, so it is not abelian\nin the commutator-theoretic sense of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"e2be868cf664b716\" href=\"?note=e2be868cf664b716\" title=\"93-df-abelian\">93-df-abelian</a>.</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"93-df-abelian","status":"resolved","id":"e2be868cf664b716","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-abelian]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-boolean-algebra","status":"resolved","id":"7087f500cc845c3b","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-boolean-algebra]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-abelian","status":"resolved","id":"e2be868cf664b716","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{AbAlg}$ is the abelian-algebra class of [[93-df-abelian]].","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-abelian","status":"resolved","id":"e2be868cf664b716","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Remark]","excerpt":"In a Boolean algebra the congruence commutator is meet, hence\n$[\\nabla_{\\mathbf A},\\nabla_{\\mathbf A}]_{\\mathbf A}=\\nabla_{\\mathbf A}$.  For a\nnontrivial algebra this is not $\\Delta_{\\mathbf A}$, so it is not abelian\nin the commutator-theoretic sense of [[93-df-abelian]].","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathrm{BooleanAlg}_{93}(\\mathbf A)","display":false},{"tex":"\\exists a,b\\in|\\mathbf A|\\;(a\\ne b)","display":false},{"tex":"[-,-]","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Con}(\\mathbf A)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{AbAlg}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{fact\\text{-}abelian\\text{-}boolean}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{BooleanAlg}_{93}(\\mathbf A)\\land\\bigl(\\exists a,b\\in|\\mathbf A|\\;(a\\ne b)\\bigr)\n\\to\\mathbf A\\notin\\mathrm{AbAlg}","display":true},{"tex":"[\\nabla_{\\mathbf A},\\nabla_{\\mathbf A}]_{\\mathbf A}=\\nabla_{\\mathbf A}","display":false},{"tex":"\\Delta_{\\mathbf A}","display":false}],"bytes":963,"backlinks":[],"outgoing":["e2be868cf664b716","7087f500cc845c3b"]}